  "version": "predicates-v4",
  "description": "Predicates a ProposalDraft may use. Wikidata mappings say which source statements can evidence each predicate: forward means the statement's entity is the assertion subject; inverse means the statement's value is the assertion subject. v2: commanded relates a person to a force (Group), not to an event. v3: authority held over a force (heldAuthorityOver) is separated from command actually exercised (commanded); evidence for one never counts for the other. v4: each predicate declares its qualifiers (context, role, time: none, optional, required, or withRole for time required only when a role is given) and its claim modes; adds the unary occurred and authorOf (22-CLAIM-QUALIFIERS.md).",
